00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
Are you looking to use returns data,

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.067
to improve your e-commerce business?

00:00:04.067 --> 00:00:05.926
Well, if you want to learn more,

00:00:05.926 --> 00:00:07.622
stick around.

00:00:12.271 --> 00:00:13.825
Did you know

00:00:13.825 --> 00:00:15.016
your returns data

00:00:15.016 --> 00:00:17.560
 is a goldmine of insightful information

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:19.543
just waiting to be uncovered?  

00:00:19.543 --> 00:00:22.370
Using an automated returns management system 

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:24.839
allows e-commerce retailers like you 

00:00:24.839 --> 00:00:26.936
to easily track their returns 

00:00:26.936 --> 00:00:29.648
and gradually create a pool of data.  

00:00:29.648 --> 00:00:32.851
That data can be leveraged to provide insight

00:00:32.851 --> 00:00:34.463
into product quality, 

00:00:34.463 --> 00:00:36.279
customer expectations, 

00:00:36.279 --> 00:00:40.192
and weaknesses in the business operational process.

00:00:40.192 --> 00:00:44.131
Method 1: Improve Your Product Descriptions 

00:00:44.131 --> 00:00:46.317
Accurate product descriptions 

00:00:46.317 --> 00:00:48.032
build trust with customers. 

00:00:48.032 --> 00:00:51.782
They help e-commerce shoppers make informed buying decisions 

00:00:51.782 --> 00:00:54.452
without even physically seeing the product. 

00:00:54.452 --> 00:00:56.051
Returns data 

00:00:56.051 --> 00:00:58.698
can be used to improve product descriptions 

00:00:58.698 --> 00:01:01.351
to accurately illustrate each item 

00:01:01.351 --> 00:01:03.854
so customers know what they’re purchasing. 

00:01:03.854 --> 00:01:08.455
Method 2: Improve the UX Website Design

00:01:08.455 --> 00:01:11.616
The same insight gathered from returns data 

00:01:11.616 --> 00:01:15.194
can also be used to improve the overall experience 

00:01:15.194 --> 00:01:17.050
of the company website.  

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:19.229
Providing an image or chart

00:01:19.229 --> 00:01:21.781
of how the product is expected to fit 

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:24.643
will boost the shopping experience for customers 

00:01:24.643 --> 00:01:26.529
by limiting confusion. 

00:01:26.529 --> 00:01:28.878
This also improves brand perception

00:01:28.878 --> 00:01:31.242
 by making the customer feel like the retailer

00:01:31.242 --> 00:01:32.860
 goes the extra mile. 

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:37.550
Method 3: Improve Your Business Operations Process 

00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:39.440
The goal of any business 

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:41.292
is to provide the best experience 

00:01:41.292 --> 00:01:42.692
for their customers.

00:01:42.692 --> 00:01:46.241
 A seamless internal process ensures that. 

00:01:46.241 --> 00:01:49.798
Analyzing metrics like average fulfillment time 

00:01:49.798 --> 00:01:52.434
can be used to pinpoint and fix problems 

00:01:52.434 --> 00:01:54.662
with staffing, resources, 

00:01:54.662 --> 00:01:56.851
operating times, etc. 

00:01:56.851 --> 00:01:58.740
to ensure all customers are

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:00.952
 getting their orders on time. 

00:02:00.952 --> 00:02:04.755
Method 4: Learn More About Your Customers

00:02:04.755 --> 00:02:07.635
Providing the best experience to your customers

00:02:07.635 --> 00:02:09.978
is always going to be a top priority. 

00:02:09.978 --> 00:02:11.553
When an e-commerce merchant

00:02:11.553 --> 00:02:13.518
knows nothing about their customers,   

00:02:13.518 --> 00:02:16.406
this task becomes close to impossible.

00:02:16.406 --> 00:02:19.168
That’s where returns data comes into play. 

00:02:19.168 --> 00:02:21.767
Analyzing customer returns behavior 

00:02:21.767 --> 00:02:23.733
using the RFM (recency, frequency, monetary) Model, 

00:02:23.733 --> 00:02:25.956
merchants can segment customers 

00:02:25.956 --> 00:02:27.405
into key clusters

00:02:27.405 --> 00:02:30.489
 and form a more personalized marketing strategy, 

00:02:30.489 --> 00:02:34.542
which will ultimately increase the customer lifetime value. 

00:02:34.542 --> 00:02:38.885
Method 5: Reduce Your Retail Return Rates 

00:02:38.885 --> 00:02:42.083
The final and most obvious way returns data

00:02:42.083 --> 00:02:44.953
can be used to make profitable business decisions 

00:02:44.953 --> 00:02:47.206
is by reducing return rates. 

00:02:47.206 --> 00:02:50.740
You should want your products to stay in the hands of your customers. 

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:52.909
While everything mentioned above

00:02:52.909 --> 00:02:55.015
 will help to reduce return rates, 

00:02:55.015 --> 00:02:57.367
our giant pool of returns data

00:02:57.367 --> 00:02:59.456
 from retailers across industries 

00:02:59.456 --> 00:03:00.918
lets us make discoveries

00:03:00.918 --> 00:03:02.517
 that would be hard to uncover 

00:03:02.517 --> 00:03:04.825
if you were just looking at the returns data

00:03:04.825 --> 00:03:06.288
from your company. 

00:03:06.288 --> 00:03:08.697
We’ve uncovered some valuable insight 

00:03:08.697 --> 00:03:10.454
on reducing return rates: 

00:03:10.454 --> 00:03:13.106
Offering warranties as a return type 

00:03:13.106 --> 00:03:16.160
reduces the refund rate by 10%.

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:18.668
Returns are becoming more popular 

00:03:18.668 --> 00:03:21.047
as more and more people shop online. 

00:03:21.047 --> 00:03:23.933
But those returns aren’t a detrimental part 

00:03:23.933 --> 00:03:25.824
of e-commerce business. 

00:03:25.824 --> 00:03:27.840
Customer returns behavior 

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:30.992
can be analyzed to identify which parts of the business 

00:03:30.992 --> 00:03:33.489
can be improved to reduce return rates 

00:03:33.489 --> 00:03:36.402
and increase the loyalty of customers.  

